WEBVTT

00:41:59.625 --> 00:42:01.893
one of the best things
that a mentor did for me

00:42:01.917 --> 00:42:05.934
was tear apart the first 37 pages
of the paper I had spent my whole year on.

00:42:05.958 --> 00:42:08.851
And then tell me,
'There's a gem on page 38.'

00:42:08.875 --> 00:42:11.559
And that tough love
changed the trajectory of my career.

00:42:11.583 --> 00:42:14.268
And I made a commitment
at that point to pay it forward.

00:42:14.292 --> 00:42:16.643
And so when I tell you
what I'm about to tell you,

00:42:16.667 --> 00:42:19.893
I do it out of what I hope is
some version of long-term kindness

00:42:19.917 --> 00:42:22.393
that I care about
your future success enough

00:42:22.417 --> 00:42:26.268
that I'm willing to potentially
hurt your feelings in the present."

00:42:26.292 --> 00:42:30.208
And I think I've just taken for granted
that people know that's true.